      "text": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef main():\n    # Memory-map the input to avoid loading the whole file at once unnecessarily\n    X_mm = np.load('vectors_secondary.npy', mmap_mode='r')\n    n, d = X_mm.shape\n\n    # Convert to float64 for numerically stable dot products; this is only\n    # 8000*1024*8 bytes ~= 64MB, which is small.\n    X = np.asarray(X_mm, dtype=np.float64)\n\n    # Precompute squared norms of each row.\n    norms = np.einsum('ij,ij->i', X, X)\n\n    total = 0.0\n    block = 400  # tune to balance memory and speed; block*n*8 bytes per temp matrix\n\n    for start in range(0, n, block):\n        end = min(start + block, n)\n        Xi = X[start:end]                      # (b, d)\n        dot = Xi @ X.T                         # (b, n) float64\n        d2 = norms[start:end, None] + norms[None, :] - 2.0 * dot\n        # Numerical noise can make small negatives; clip them to zero.\n        np.maximum(d2, 0.0, out=d2)\n        np.sqrt(d2, out=d2)\n        total += d2.sum()\n\n        # free explicitly to help garbage collector on large temp arrays\n        del dot, d2, Xi\n\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total:.10f}\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
